;; Verified public-register citations for the legal entity archived by this repository.
;;
;; Every row is checked live by tools/verify_citations.cljs:
;;   * GET :cite/url must answer HTTP 2xx
;;   * :cite/expect-substring must appear in the response body
;;
;; A URL that cannot be fetched, or whose body no longer carries the claim, is a
;; DRIFT and fails the gate. Nothing is recorded here that was not retrieved.
;;
;; THREE independent authorities are cited, not one:
;;   * GLEIF, the global LEI system
;;   * the United States, via the SEC's EDGAR submissions API (Banco Santander is
;;     a foreign private issuer, NYSE ticker SAN, CIK 0000891478)
;;   * the issuer itself, at its own published website www.santander.com -- the
;;     legal notice this repository archives (80-data/public/tos.journal.edn)
;;
;; WHY NO SPANISH STATE REGISTER IS CITED DIRECTLY. GLEIF names RA000535 -- the
;; Tax Agency, Agencia Tributaria (AEAT) -- as BOTH the register of record and
;; the validation authority for this entity (rows gleif-registered-at and
;; gleif-validated-at), and the registered-as A39000013 is the Spanish tax
;; number (NIF), not a company-register number. AEAT publishes no per-entity
;; GET URL: NIF census lookups run behind certificate-authenticated flows
;; (sede.agenciatributaria.gob.es answered 200 to this gate on 2026-08-22, but
;; only with its portal page). The company-law register the issuer itself
;; names -- the Santander Mercantile Registry, sheet 286, folio 64, Companies
;; Book no. 5, entry 1 -- publishes per-entity data behind paid/POST flows at
;; registradores.org (top page 200 to this gate, 2026-08-22; no stable
;; per-entity GET URL). The Banco de Espana credit-institution register (code
;; 0049) likewise offers no stable per-entity GET URL this gate can replay.
;; What the catalog does instead is cite the issuer's OWN legal notice, which
;; prints the tax number, the registered office, the Banco de Espana code and
;; the Mercantile Registry entry in a single sentence (rows issuer-bde-number,
;; issuer-seat, issuer-tax-number, issuer-mercantile), and corroborate the
;; entity through a second STATE authority that does answer on stable URLs:
;;
;;   GLEIF says the legal seat is PASEO DE PEREDA 9-12, SANTANDER, ES-S, 39004
;;   (rows gleif-address, gleif-city, gleif-postal) -> the issuer prints
;;   'registered office at Paseo de Pereda, 9-12, Santander'. GLEIF records
;;   registeredAs A39000013 -> the issuer prints 'tax number A-39000013'.
;;   GLEIF records the legal name BANCO SANTANDER S.A. -> the SEC prints
;;   Banco Santander, S.A. as the registrant name, incorporated in Spain,
;;   NYSE ticker SAN. The SEC and GLEIF never consulted each other.
;;
;; ONE HONEST WRINKLE, SO A READER DOES NOT MISREAD IT AS DRIFT: the SEC's
;; business address is CIUDAD GRUPO SANTANDER, BOADILLA DEL MONTE, MADRID
;; 28660 -- the operational corporate centre -- while GLEIF and the issuer's
;; legal notice both give the REGISTERED office in the city of Santander.
;; Both are true; they are different facts (rows sec-street, sec-street2).
;; Note also gleif-corroboration: this record is PARTIALLY_CORROBORATED, not
;; FULLY_CORROBORATED. The catalog records what GLEIF says, not more.
;;
;; WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT CITED. GLEIF's nextRenewalDate and lastUpdateDate
;; move by construction; a row on either would go red on schedule while saying
;; nothing about the entity. The GLEIF ISIN mapping carries 6,189 ISINs for
;; this serial note issuer and moves by construction too; measured 2026-08-22,
;; the endpoint's filter[isin] parameter is not honored (it returned the full
;; unfiltered set), so no per-ISIN row is possible and no count row is wanted.
;; NYSE quote pages sit behind JS/POST-gated APIs and are not citations.
;;
;; :cite/row-kind is the honest part of this catalog and should be read before
;; the claims:
;;
;;   :identity   the substring names this entity, its identifiers, or a specific
;;               related legal entity (two of the 79 direct children, the BIC,
;;               the MICs). Point the URL at a different company and the row
;;               fails.
;;   :attribute  the substring is TRUE OF THIS ENTITY BUT NOT ONLY OF IT (status
;;               ACTIVE, country ES, SIC 6029, fiscal year 1231). Such a row can
;;               survive a swap to a similar company. It is recorded because it
;;               is checked and true, not because it identifies.
;;   :definition the row resolves a code used by another row (RA000535, ELF
;;               5RDO, the managing LOU). It says the named register, legal
;;               form or LEI issuer exists; it says nothing about Santander.
;;
;; Of the entries below, 29 are :identity, 26 are :attribute and 8 are
;; :definition. A reader who treats all 63 as identifying would overstate what
;; this catalog proves -- which is the error this field exists to prevent.
;;
;; Substrings are taken from the RAW response body and were each checked against
;; the fetched bytes before this file was written (2026-08-22, GLEIF golden copy
;; of 2026-08-21). The child-count row goes red when GLEIF adds or removes a
;; relationship; that is correct DRIFT, not a false alarm. GLEIF escapes URL
;; slashes in its JSON (es\/39000013, https:\/\/...); the ocid and lou-website
;; rows match that raw escaped form deliberately. The issuer's legal-notice
;; <title> begins with a literal space; the row keeps it.
{:catalog/subject
 #:company{:legal-name "BANCO SANTANDER S.A."
           :lei "5493006QMFDDMYWIAM13"
           :jurisdiction "ES"
           :registered-at "RA000535"
           :registered-as "A39000013"
           :legal-form "5RDO"
           :website "https://www.santander.com/en/home"}
